# TRACKED HERE, IN THE GAME'S OWN REPO, AND NOT HAND-COPIED INTO THE GAMES SITE.
#
# It lived in games-alphazone/public/console-room/ for the first four deploys,
# which meant every one of them had a step that read "now put the .htaccess
# back, because `cp -r dist` will not carry it" — and nothing visibly fails
# when that step is missed. The site just serves yesterday's build, and every
# check against it passes. Ben lost an afternoon to exactly that on Green
# Hollow on 2026-09-10.
#
# Vite copies `public/` into `dist/` verbatim, so `cp -r dist` now carries it
# and the hand step is gone. This is what `longstep` already does and the
# reason that game has never been the one that bit.
#
# Same reason as public/burgerbarn/.htaccess, and it is worth restating rather
# than cross-referencing, because a file that only says "see the other one" is
# the file nobody reads.
#
# The host sends NO Cache-Control on index.html, so browsers fall back to
# HEURISTIC caching — roughly a tenth of the file's age since last-modified —
# and quietly keep serving a stale document that points at stale bundle hashes.
# A hard refresh does not always beat it. Ben lost an afternoon to this on
# Green Hollow on 2026-09-10, reporting a bug that was already fixed while
# every check against the live site passed.
#
# index.html is the ONE file that must always be revalidated: it is the map to
# every hashed bundle. The bundles are content-addressed (index-<hash>.js), so
# a name never means two different files and they can be cached forever.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  <FilesMatch "\.html$">
    Header set Cache-Control "no-cache, must-revalidate, max-age=0"
  </FilesMatch>
  <FilesMatch "\.(js|css|png|jpg|svg|woff2?)$">
    Header set Cache-Control "public, max-age=31536000, immutable"
  </FilesMatch>
</IfModule>
